dive for Thursday, October 29. Sweden's chatbot block is about contracts, not countries.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:50.300
I'm Bella. Like the briefing, it is written and read by AI from public sources.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:58.040
On Monday, October 26, Sweden's government offices blocked chat GPT and clawed on staff

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:02.900
work computers. This is the body that supports the prime minister's office and every ministry.

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:05.980
Staff are being sent to Microsoft's co-pilot instead.

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:10.900
Six days earlier, the U.S. Department of Homeland Security published an order

00:11:10.900 --> 00:11:13.480
removing DeepSeek from federal civilian systems.

00:11:14.040 --> 00:11:16.700
But the two side by side and the headline writes itself,

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:19.180
Governments are walling off foreign AI.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:20.820
Is that true, though?

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:25.100
The first reports we saw gave no reason for the Swedish move.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:30.500
The reporting since then, which traces back to Sveria's radio, does give a reason.

00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:33.200
and the reason is not where the chatbot comes from.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:36.260
So today's question is narrower and more useful.

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:38.880
When a government shuts out an AI tool,

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.940
is it doing so over data handling, security, or politics?

00:11:43.540 --> 00:11:47.420
And what does each of those grounds mean for a company trying to sell to the public sector?

00:11:49.380 --> 00:11:51.280
Start with what Sweden actually did.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:56.240
It blocked the web versions of ChatGPT and Claude, the sites you open in a browser.

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:58.060
It did not ban the models.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:12:01.440
A limited number of staff can still reach both through Intric,

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:04.560
a Stockholm platform for building AI assistance.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:08.020
Intric says its platform runs on servers in Sweden,

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:10.360
with no need for foreign cloud firms.

00:12:11.020 --> 00:12:14.340
Copilot was approved because, in the government office's words,

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:16.800
they had checked that tool and made it safer.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:19.560
And here's what makes it interesting.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:24.520
Microsoft has said Copilot will continue to be powered by OpenAI's latest models.

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:29.960
Microsoft has also added anthropic models to Microsoft 365 Copilot.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:35.320
So the same model families can stay in the building while the consumer front door gets locked.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:36.860
An analogy helps.

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:41.680
Think of a ministry that bans staff from emailing documents to their personal Gmail.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:44.360
Nobody reads that as a ban on Google.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:49.420
It's a rule about which channel has a signed contract, an audit trail,

00:12:49.800 --> 00:12:51.700
and an admin who can change the settings.

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:54.220
Sweden's block works the same way.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:13:00.500
The digitalization director, Mikkel Wedderkranz, wrote on the staff intranet that using AI services

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:04.680
without formal contracts can have consequences for information security.

00:13:05.400 --> 00:13:08.760
He added that they had seen several examples of problematic use,

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.620
covering both what was typed in and how the answers were handled.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:16.520
The U.S. DeepSeek order works on a different principle.

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:21.140
It was issued under the Federal Acquisition Supply Chain Security Act of 2018,

00:13:21.140 --> 00:13:25.920
a law that lets the government exclude a vendor it judges to be a supply chain risk.

00:13:26.520 --> 00:13:28.200
The issue there is who the vendor is.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:32.600
DHS argues that sensitive information from U.S. government users

00:13:32.600 --> 00:13:35.940
could be reachable by Chinese authorities under Chinese law.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:41.280
The order covers DeepSeek's own products and third-party products built on DeepSeek.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:46.900
No contract fixes that because the objection is to the vendor's legal home.

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.340
So the two moves have a different mechanism.

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.920
Sweden is saying, go through a contracted channel.

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:56.720
The US is saying, not this vendor through any channel.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:13:59.980
Here's what is established.

00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:06.280
The Swedish bloc took effect October 26 and covers browser access across the government offices.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:11.340
That comes from Sveria's radio's reporting and the director's own internet note,

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:13.140
which several outlets quote.

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:19.300
Sweden's tax agency and the National Board of Institutional Care already had similar blocs.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:22.880
The enforcement authority was preparing its own decision.

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:27.660
An internal review at the Swedish Transport Administration earlier,

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:34.120
this year found roughly 10 AI services being used in what was described as a widespread and risky way.

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:37.320
On the U.S. side, the record is primary.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:42.980
The order was dated July 24 and published in the Federal Register on October 20.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:47.680
It applies to civilian agencies such as Treasury, State, and Justice.

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:56.920
The Congressional Research Service notes that the Defense Department and the Director of National Intelligence issued their own orders on September 8.

00:14:57.640 --> 00:15:01.320
DHS wrote that DeepSeq's models present multiple threat vectors.

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:07.340
DeepSeq's own privacy policy says it stores users' personal data in the People's Republic of China.

00:15:07.980 --> 00:15:09.580
There's also a third data point.

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:16.920
In February, the European Parliament's IT department turned off built-in AI features on lawmakers' devices.

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:21.300
That covered Copilot along with ChatGPT and Claude.

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:26.220
Its email said it could not guarantee the security of data uploaded to AI companies' servers.

00:15:26.960 --> 00:15:28.560
Now for what is claimed but not shown.

00:15:29.120 --> 00:15:33.400
We have no examples of what Swedish staff actually leaked, only that problems were seen.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:35.460
We don't know how many people are affected.

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:40.160
We also don't know what Copilot settings were changed, or whether data stays in Sweden.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:45.480
On the US side, the order does not define what DeepSeek implementations means.

00:15:45.480 --> 00:15:50.000
Does a self-hosted copy of an open-weight deep-seek model count?

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:51.660
What about a fine-tune of one?

00:15:52.120 --> 00:15:55.400
The order doesn't say, and the CRS summary doesn't settle it.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:56.640
One more caution.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:16:01.740
The idea that U.S. law lets American authorities demand chatbot user data

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:04.420
was TechCrunch's framing of the parliament's story.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:08.880
The parliament's own email didn't say it, so the evidence is lopsided.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:13.000
The contract and data handling reading for Sweden is well supported.

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:17.020
A political reading is something we'd be inferring,

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:19.400
not something anyone in Sweden stated.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:23.620
Each reading starts from the same facts.

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:26.540
The AGI forward reading focuses on cost.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:29.100
If frontier models keep improving fast,

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:33.820
a ministry that limits staff to one approved assistant gives up capability every quarter.

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:39.040
On that view, blocks like this push usage into shadow AI on personal phones,

00:16:39.480 --> 00:16:41.660
which is exactly the leak they were meant to stop.

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:47.920
the a realist reading says this is ordinary it governance catching up an audit found about 10

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:54.400
unmanaged services the organization then picked one under contract and blocked the rest nothing

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:59.820
about it depends on what the models can do the market reading points to who won microsoft already

